course: dictionary
lesson: 277
title: Names and capital letters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Amelia is a name. A name is a special kind of noun for a particular person, place or thing, and it always starts with a capital letter. You will see Amelia in stories and maths problems, such as «Amelia has 12 stickers.» Here Amelia is just the character's name, so you do not need to look it up in a dictionary to know what it means.
explain: Names can also come with a story. In history lessons you may learn about Amelia Earhart, a famous pilot. She was the first woman to fly alone across the Atlantic Ocean, and later she disappeared while trying to fly around the world.
explain: Context helps you read names too. «In Dublin, Amelia's stepbrother tells her, "You're not my real sister, ye sap." It hurts.» The place name Dublin tells you where the story happens, and the words "It hurts" tell you how Amelia feels. Ye is an older or regional way of saying you, and the clues show it is unkind.
fact: Amelia is a girl's first name.
fact: Amelia is very popular in the UK, Australia and other English-speaking countries.
fact: Names always start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
fact: Short forms of Amelia include Millie, Amy and Mia.
fact: Amelia Earhart was an American pilot and the first woman to fly alone across the Atlantic Ocean.
exercise: «Amelia has 12 stickers.» What kind of word is Amelia in this sentence? | A place | *A name of a person | A sticker | A number
exercise: Who was Amelia Earhart? | A famous cook from Sydney | A ship captain from Bristol | *An American pilot who was the first woman to fly alone across the Atlantic | A queen of England
exercise: Which of these is a short form of Amelia? | Bristol | Sophie | *Mia | Dublin
test: Why does Amelia start with a capital letter? | Because it is a colour | Because it is a sad word | Because it is very long | *Because it is a name, and names begin with a capital letter
test: In «Amelia in Bristol told her baby brother that the moon follows only him», which word is a place? | brother | *Bristol | moon | Amelia
exam: Which fact about Amelia Earhart is true? | She was a famous cook from Sydney | *She disappeared while trying to fly around the world | She wrote the first English dictionary | She was a queen of England
